<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Germany and Central Europe</p><h1 class="st-title">Canton of Unterwalden</h1><p class="st-meta">1291 CE – 1798 CE · capital Sarnen and Stans</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">One of the three founding cantons of the Swiss Confederacy, a mountain community on Lake Lucerne that was always split into two self-governing halves.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The valleys south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-lucerne">Lake Lucerne</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obwalden">Obwalden</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sarnen">Sarnen</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nidwalden">Nidwalden</a> around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/stans">Stans</a>, were rural communities under scattered lordships, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a>. Nidwalden swore the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/federal-charter-of-1291">Federal Charter of 1291</a> with the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-uri">Canton of Uri</a> and the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/canton-of-schwyz">Canton of Schwyz</a>, and Obwalden soon joined, so Unterwalden counted among the three original forest cantons of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/old-swiss-confederacy">Old Swiss Confederacy</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Each half held its own <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/landsgemeinde">Landsgemeinde</a>, an open-air assembly of free men that elected officials and passed laws, and the two shared a single seat at the federal <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tagsatzung">Diet</a>. The economy rested on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cattle">cattle</a>, cheese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mercenary">mercenary</a> service abroad. Unterwalden remained firmly Catholic during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> and stood with the other inner cantons against <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/canton-of-zurich">Zürich</a> and Bern.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>When <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> imposed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/helvetic-republic">Helvetic Republic</a> in 1798, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nidwalden">Nidwalden</a> resisted and was crushed in September 1798 with heavy loss of civilian life. After 1803 the two halves re-emerged and today survive as the separate cantons of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/obwalden">Obwalden</a> and Nidwalden.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/canton-of-unterwalden.jpg" alt="Canton of Unterwalden" width="320" height="320"><figcaption>Image: Original: Unknown author Vector: Dbachmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Old_flag_of_Unterwalden.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1291 CE – 1798 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sarnen and Stans</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Catholicism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Swiss German</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/switzerland">Switzerland</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Unterwalden, Obwalden and Nidwalden</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1544&amp;focus=canton-of-unterwalden" aria-label="Canton of Unterwalden on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4875 531 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Canton of Unterwalden lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5195 787L5186 782M5195 787L5188 772"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5186 782h0M5188 772h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5195 787h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5195 787h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its recorded location. <a href="/atlas?year=1544&amp;focus=canton-of-unterwalden">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
